1. रुज् cl. 6. P. (Dhātup. xxviii, 123) रुज॑ति (ep. also ˚ते; pf. रुरो॑ज, RV. &c. &c.; aor. 2. sg. रोक्, VS.; रुक्, MaitrS.; अरौक्षीत् Gr.; fut. रोक्ता, रोक्ष्यति, ib.; inf. -रु॑जे, RV.; ind.p. रुक्त्वा॑, -रु॑ज्य, Br.),
to break, break open, dash to pieces, shatter, destroy, RV. &c. &c.;
to cause pain, afflict, injure (with acc. or gen.; cf. Pāṇ. ii, 3, 54), VS. &c. &c.:
Caus. रोजयति (aor. अरूरुजत्), to cause to break &c.;
to strike upon (loc.), BhP.;
 (cl. 10. Dhātup. xxxiii, 129) to hurt, injure, kill:
Desid. रुरुक्षति Gr. (see रुरुक्ष॑णि) :
Intens. रोरुज्यते, रोरोक्ति, Gr.
